% The keys and hashes of the policy, as the source writes them.
the public key of the primary key is "[a5c6b76e/48'/1'/0'/2']tpubDF5861hj6vR3iJr3aPjGJz4rNbqDCRujQ21mczzKT5SiedaQqNVgHC8HT9ceyxvMFRoPMx4P6HAcL3NZrUPhRUbwCyj3TKSa64bAfnE3sLh/<0;1>/*".

the public key of the recovery key is "[c477fd13/48'/1'/0'/2']tpubDFn7iPbFqGrTQ2aRACNsUK1MXQR4Z6dYfU2nD1WA9ifSaia642j3Wah4n5pBUEpERNWGJsyv3Dv5qwBabC9TLQrwSboKzukw9wmurGu7XVH/<0;1>/*".

% The spending paths of the policy.
rule primary with provenance the Liana recovery guide,
        confer "Your Liana wallet descriptor is probably of the form":
the coin can be spent if
    the witness contains a signature by the primary key.

rule recovery with provenance the Liana recovery guide,
        confer "Your Liana wallet descriptor is probably of the form":
the coin can be spent if
    the witness contains a signature by the recovery key
    and the coin has been confirmed for a number N blocks
    and N >= 3.

% The age of the coin, which the relative timelocks (older) measure.
rule coin_age_in_blocks:
the coin has been confirmed for a number N blocks if
    the coin was confirmed in block a height H
    and the spending transaction is in block a height M
    and N = M - H.

scenario recovery is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path recovery — the path needs: a coin 3 blocks old, a signature by the recovery key
    the witness contains a signature by the recovery key.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850003.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario recovery_without_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path recovery without requirement 1 — the path needs: a coin 3 blocks old, a signature by the recovery key
    the witness contains a signature by the recovery key.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850002.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario recovery_without_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path recovery without requirement 2 — the path needs: a coin 3 blocks old, a signature by the recovery key
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850003.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario primary is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path primary — the path needs: a signature by the primary key
    the witness contains a signature by the primary key.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850000.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario primary_without_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path primary without requirement 1 — the path needs: a signature by the primary key
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850000.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario no_witness is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % an empty witness
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850000.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario flip_now is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, no delay passed
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850000.
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness contains a signature by the primary key"]].

scenario flip_after_delays is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, every delay passed
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850003.
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness contains a signature by the primary key"], ["add: the witness contains a signature by the recovery key"]].

scenario lost_the_primary_key is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of the primary key lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by the recovery key.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850003.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the coin was confirmed in block 850000"], ["remove: the spending transaction is in block 850003"], ["remove: the witness contains a signature by the recovery key"]].

scenario lost_the_recovery_key is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of the recovery key lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by the primary key.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850003.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the witness contains a signature by the primary key"]].

scenario chain_recovery is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at the refusal of attempt path_1:
    % the chain refused the spend: non-BIP68-final
    the witness contains a signature by the recovery key.
    the coin was confirmed in block 122322.
    the spending transaction is in block 122322.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario chain_recovery_without_1 is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at the refusal of attempt path_1_without_1:
    % the chain refused the spend: non-BIP68-final
    the coin was confirmed in block 122322.
    the spending transaction is in block 122322.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario chain_primary is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at transaction f980a95dfc7d411f3db9ff055c37c613cee42b19844f876c305e845b419db3d6:
    % the chain accepted the spend: transaction f980a95dfc7d411f3db9ff055c37c613cee42b19844f876c305e845b419db3d6
    the witness contains a signature by the primary key.
    the coin was confirmed in block 122322.
    the spending transaction is in block 122322.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

query spendable is:
    the coin can be spent.

query flip_spend is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        the coin can be spent.

query flip_block is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        it is not the case that the coin can be spent.

query keys is:
    the public key of which key is which text.

the view custody explainer is:
    the title is "Who can spend this coin: A Liana wallet: a primary key, or a recovery key after a delay".
    the case is a scenario, with the documents it is stated in.
    the facts about "the witness" are
        the witness contains a signature by a key.
    the facts about "the timelocks" are
        the coin was confirmed in block a height,
        the spending transaction is in block a height.
    the result is whether the coin can be spent.
    the result shows its reasons.
    the result shows its citations.
    the result can be flipped, as "What would let this coin be spent?".
    the flip keeps the coin was confirmed in block a height,
        the spending transaction is in block a height.

